; walk-sdx — the note delay, and the note that never sounds.
;
; `SD3` sounds three ticks into the row, `SD0` behaves as `SD1`, and
; `SD6` is the row's whole tick count, so that note has no onset at all.
; Onsets come out in (row, channel) order, which is time order within a
; channel and not across them.
;
; The fixture's patterns are shorter than IT 2.14's floor of 32 rows, so
; the reader warns once per pattern and honours them — which is what puts
; this row map beside plan 06's hand computation instead of beside a
; padded one.
(read)
(walk)
